        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How do you turn on a NordicTrack treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Plug the cord into a surge suppressor on a grounded outlet, then press the power switch on the frame near the power cord into the reset (I) position. Stand on the foot rails, clip the safety key to your waistband and insert the key into the console. An LED console lights after a moment; a touchscreen can take up to a few minutes to boot.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Where is the on/off switch on a NordicTrack treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On the treadmill frame near the power cord, which on most NordicTrack machines is low on the front of the base. It is a rocker switch with an off position and an on position that the manuals call reset and mark I. There is no power button on the console.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Why won’t my NordicTrack treadmill turn on?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Check, in order, that the cord and surge suppressor are plugged in and working, that the outlet works with a lamp, that the safety key is fully inserted, and that the power switch has not tripped. If the switch protrudes, wait five minutes and press it back in. A new LED-console model may also need activating at iFIT.com/activate.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you turn on a NordicTrack without the safety key?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The belt will not run without the key in the console, and on most models the console stays dark too. If the display lights without the key, the console is in demo mode, a store display setting you can turn off. If you have lost the key, order the correct replacement for your model number.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How long does a NordicTrack touchscreen take to turn on?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              NordicTrack's X22i manual says it may take up to a few minutes for the console to be ready, and the first start, or a start after a long gap, can take longer if a firmware update runs. Do not switch off or unplug during an update; the machine restarts itself when it finishes.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do I need iFIT to turn on a NordicTrack treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. The power switch and safety key turn it on, and every NordicTrack has a manual mode that runs the belt with no membership. Touch Manual Start or press Start on a touchscreen, or press Manual and then Start on an LED console. iFIT adds trainer-led and automatically controlled workouts on top.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Should I unplug my NordicTrack after every use?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              NordicTrack's manuals say yes: remove the key, press the power switch to off and unplug the cord when you finish, because otherwise the electrical components may wear prematurely. The exception is a firmware update in progress, which must be left to finish.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
